  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "rp_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": -524,
        "y": 0
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Reaction Painter\n\nPaint chemistry: drag on the preview to drop chemical B, and watch it react and spread into coral, cells or fingerprints. Keys 1–7 switch the reaction (coral, mitosis, fingerprints, worms, maze, spots, waves) while it runs, P cycles the colours, R (or Reset) wipes the dish back to the three seed rings. Speed sets how many reaction steps run a frame.\n\nHow it works: Simulation in reaction mode (Gray–Scott). Its `paint` points are a little brush of seven points round the mouse, kept only while the button is down (Sublist keep-where). The `preset` pin is wired from Lookup over the preset names, picked by the last number key; the colour ramp is one of four palettes picked with Lookup group-at.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 250
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rp_mouse",
      "defType": "input/mouse",
      "position": {
        "x": 37,
        "y": 400
      },
      "params": {}
    },
